% TM-100 PDF page 4, printed folio 2. Section 1 (2) ESP: the syntax of an ESP class
% definition as printed (a grammar schema, not SIMPOS code). Transcribed by eye from
% 300dpi crops. NOTE: an earlier pass listed "class object (p4)"; no class 'object'
% listing exists on this page -- only this schema.
% Prose following: "The inheritance part defines the super classes which this class
% inherits.  A list of the super classes can be specified.  Their order is relevant,
% because the operation definitions given in these classes are OR'ed in this order.
% This class itself can be specified in this list. ... The local part defines the
% predicates which can be called only within this class."

        class  <class name>  has
            [ <nature definition> ; ]              ..... inheritance
            { <class slot definition> ; }          ...
            { <class clause definition> ; }        ..:.. class
      [ instance
            { <instance slot definition> ; }       ...
            { <instance clause definition> ; } ]   ..:.. instance
      [ local
            { <local clause definition> ; } ]      ..... local
        end.
